{"success":true,"data":{"id":"battletech-simulator-arxdo2-mrz2ryw73uq","title":"Movement Rules Fix - Facing costs, PSR, MASC, TSM","description":"Movement Rules Fix - Facing costs, PSR, MASC, TSM.\n\nFIXES NEEDED:\n1. Facing change costs in pathfinding - Add 1 MP per hexside turn during BFS in getValidMoves(). Currently facing changes are free.\n\n2. PSR gyro modifier - Single gyro hit = +3 PSR modifier (not 0). Code at PSRCalculator.js:60 has baseModifier: 0 for gyro.hits === 1.\n\n3. Missing PSR triggers:\n   - Overheating (heat  while running/jumping)\n   - Physical attacks received (kicked, charged, DFA'd)\n   - Standing up (with leg damage modifiers)\n\n4. Fall damage formula - Multiply by levels fallen. Current: ceil(tonnage/10). Correct: ceil(tonnage/10) * levelsFallen.\n\n5. Fall damage location - Roll on hit location table once per 5-point damage cluster, with automatic crit roll.\n\n6. MASC failure mechanics - Target increases by +2 each consecutive turn active (turn 2 = 5, turn 3 = 7, ...). Use mascTurnsActive in calculation.\n\n7. MASC failure damage - Apply leg actuator damage on failure, not just deactivation.\n\n8. Level change restriction - Prohibit walking/running into hex 3+ levels higher (only jump-capable).\n\n9. Water depth modifiers - Depth 1 = +0 PSR, depth 2 = +1, depth 3+ = +2.\n\nTEST: Write tests for facing costs, PSR modifiers, MASC failure scaling, fall damage formula.","status":"open","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2026-07-24T15:08:33.511Z","updated_at":"2026-07-24T15:09:04.318Z","parent_id":"battletech-simulator-arxdo2-mrz2ryu6vqj","dependencies":[],"metadata":{}}}
